# Lab red-team policy (Cybersec Phase-1)

Adversarial LLM / agent eval tools are **authorized lab only**. No LIVE Discord, no unauthorized targets.

## Authorization

- Written scope (owned lab, bug-bounty rules, or engagement letter) before running FuzzyAI, AHA, cryptex, Senthex, OpenART/EMHA, PIMiner, ARIA instruction-backdoor RT, Trident-class DRL red, or similar.
- OpenART (`raw-sources/repos/OpenART`) is **AGPL-3.0** — lab sandbox only; do not network-serve or ship into prod without license review.
- Prefer Docker-sandboxed victims; never point autoresearch red-team loops at third-party production.
- Kid-safety / social-engineering pages are for parent/teacher/LE context — not offensive grooming research.
- AirKey-class Wi-Fi CSI + acoustic PIN inference: **authorized physical/wireless lab only** — no LIVE/unauthorized eavesdrop.

## Eval discipline

- Report dual metrics where relevant (overall ASR vs full/phase ASR); do not optimize a single ASR number.
- Respect evidential ceilings — stop claiming more certainty than the eval design supports (`ai-redteam-evidential-limits`).
- InferScale / KV-injection: treat shared-prefix or cache-poison findings as security bugs in agent infra, not as free speedups to ship unchecked.

## Training data / fine-tune

- Run DataShield-class risky-finetune filters in lab before any Cemini/TipDrop fine-tune on scraped corpora.
- Do **not** install OC-GRPO or other GRPO trainer stacks as “wired” harness — REFERENCE/paper repro only.
- Notes-to-self / experiential memory clones: lab only; reconstruct before inject (see federation MemHarness rule).

## Aug 7 batch (ARIA 2608.05659 · taxonomy 2608.06246 · NL-LTL 2608.06287 · HarnessOpt 2608.06301)

- **ARIA** — red-team system-prompt / custom-instruction surfaces (instruction backdoors), not only weight poison or prompt injection; require stealth + clean utility + ASR together; REFERENCE only (no public code); lab / written scope; no LIVE third-party customization platforms.
- **Post-training taxonomy** — when changing local or released models, log six axes: mechanism / goal / data / persistence / scope / model-type; pair with DataShield + Gradient Immunity for open-weight release paths; survey vocabulary only.
- **NL→LTL** — LLM drafts for security/mission-critical LTL only with human + solver verify; prefer pass@k / consistency over single-shot; no automatic policy authority.
- **HarnessOpt-Bench** — treat harness optimization as its own metric under budgeted held-out eval + version audit; ban unbounded auto-optimize of prod/LIVE harness (HITL + rollback); no clone until public artifact + LICENSE.
- **K254 keystores (lab)** — keep signing/SSH/API private keys out of agent-readable memory / workspace / env; PKCS#11 or OS-isolated handles; SoftHSM = repro only; authorized scope only.
- **K255 READ (lab)** — long lab runbooks / reports → grep · outline · bounded read with citable line ranges; no opaque RAG.
- **K258 PTC (lab)** — sandboxed abliterated agents → typed stubs + scripts for multi-tool fan-out; schema-bound / gated; no TrajDebug runtime.
- **K266 ShieldAI taxonomy map (lab)** — when stocking OSS eval/guardrail/observability tools, map candidates to an explicit risk taxonomy (MIT extended / ShieldAI matrices); expect governance/legal/market gaps that tooling alone cannot close; HITL + org process required. REFERENCE clone `raw-sources/repos/ShieldAI` (~896KB Apache-2.0) — not a runtime MCP.
